{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother","id":591553,"title":"The Wyrm / Grandmother?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T11:15:55-07:00","id":591553,"title":"The Wyrm / Grandmother?","content":"Okay.... are the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Wyrm\" target=\"_blank\">Wyrm (W:TA)</a> and <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Grandmother\" target=\"_blank\">Grandmother (W:TO)</a> one and the same?<br /> <br /> The Wyrm lies imprisoned beneath the Black Spiral Labyrinth deep within Malfeas.<br /> Grandmother lay sleeping beneath the Labyrinth above Oblivion... until a dumbass mage nuked it and woke her.<br /> Many suspect these are the same labyrinth.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm creates bane spirits loyal to it which are bent on destruction.<br /> Grandmother made the neverborn spectres, which... kinda want the same thing.<br /> <br /> People/spirits can become corrupted by banes, and in the end will assist the eventual destruction the wyrm desires.<br /> Wraiths can slowly accrue shadow, their essence becoming corrupted as part of them desires oblivion and destruction until they become spectres.<br /> Couldn't spectres be a form of bane spirit?<br /> <br /> The Wyrm wants to destroy all of reality.<br /> Grandmother wants to do that too. She's literally EATING it! Consuming the labyrinth as she pulls herself out and up, to eat everything else as she goes...<br /> <br /> Anyone see any holes in this interpretation? 'Cause I'm pretty sure this one holds together under scrutiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:29:44-07:00","id":591575,"title":"","content":"Building off that I think Lucifer and the Weaver may also have a great deal in common, being the same or related entities themselves:<br /> <br /> &quot;Weaver implanted mortals with three gifts, Dogma, Science, and Technology, in order to survive.&quot;<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Weaver\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Weaver</a><br /> <br /> It was Lucifer who went on a campaign to encourage science &amp; technology after releasing his lieutenants from the Abyss resulted in the creation of the Earthbound. The Angels were the &quot;weavers&quot; of reality, crafting it all, and they went mad with rebellion when they abandoned the creator in an effort to prevent their works from being destroyed. <br /> <br /> &quot;mythology states that the Weaver grew tired of its order being destroyed by the Wyrm, and spun its webs to imprison the Wyrm and end its destruction.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lucifer encouraged disbelief, enforcing a loss of faith and banality throughout all of the world to prevent his fellow fallen from escaping the pit. He was a major cause of the spread of banality and the effects of the weaver's spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:39:47-07:00","id":591592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother#post591553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone see any holes in this interpretation? 'Cause I'm pretty sure this one holds together under scrutiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because the Wyrm is explicitly stated to not be active in the Dark Umbra. Whiffs of taint on spectres are from coincidental relationships, read because spectres are such shitty people that they give off similar vibes. They aren't banes, though, because they lack the capacity to turn living beings into fomori when they possess them.<br /> <br /> This entire thing you're going off on has been done before, and it doesn't hold up because all of the games are designed to disagree so strongly that you'll never shave off those ill-fitting ends to make them fit without losing something from the game whose ends were just shaven off. It isn't an interconnected picture like Exalted, it's a bunch of different pictures painted by each game, which all have things that are important to them that other games either don't care about or downright just disdain. It won't add up.<br /> <br /> As for the Weaver and Lucifer, let's go back and review about the Triat being building blocks of the universe in addition to vast spiritual presences. As Supernals rather than mere Celestines, they carry far more of the cosmos on their backs, and each is absolutely necessary. You could probably scrub Lucifer out from his own game and not actually end up losing a third of what makes the universe the universe, so that one fallen angel is way, way too small to be a part of the Triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T12:24:32-07:00","id":591625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=591592#post591592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because the Wyrm is explicitly stated to not be active in the Dark Umbra. Whiffs of taint on spectres are from coincidental relationships, read because spectres are such shitty people that they give off similar vibes. They aren't banes, though, because they lack the capacity to turn living beings into fomori when they possess them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wyrm is explicitly stated to be imprisoned in Malfeas, which is in the Deep Umbra. But Malfeas is also a Near Realm (as is the Abyss). Placing Malfeas in, around, or near the Abyss and the Oblivion would not make the Wyrm active in the rest of the Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> Every shitty person doesn't sporadically light up as wyrm-tainted. It takes significantly more than that. Though I didn't know that werewolves would actively detect wyrm-taint on spectres, it was only a guess (thanks for confirming that).<br /> <br /> And I don't know what happens when a spectre attempts to possess a person! But I know that spectres can become pretty <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Nephwrack\" target=\"_blank\">warped and unnatural</a>... I suspect that's something that would be up to a Storyteller's discretion. Seeing as &quot;Banes are evil spirits in service to the Wyrm,&quot; if Grandmother can be established as associated with the Wyrm in any capacity then spectres would, in a sense, be banes.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that Grandmother, and only Grandmother, is the Wyrm. I expect it's much more complex than that, but I would pin her as one of the Wyrm's most powerful manifestations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This entire thing you're going off on has been done before, and it doesn't hold up because all of the games are designed to disagree so strongly that you'll never shave off those ill-fitting ends to make them fit without losing something from the game whose ends were just shaven off. It isn't an interconnected picture like Exalted, it's a bunch of different pictures painted by each game, which all have things that are important to them that other games either don't care about or downright just disdain. It won't add up. </div> </div> </div>I don't feel like I'm shaving anything off... especially not when you consider that some of the published materials have suggested that the earliest eras in the WoD were practically free of all banality, that would leave a much more fluid world (especially with regard to the passage of time, existence of multiple realities in the same place, etc) more like the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Flux_%28WTA%29\" target=\"_blank\">Flux</a> which would allow multiple explanations of events to be true simultaneously. Speaking of multiple right answers.... the minds behind World of Darkness <i>frequently</i> wrote multiple answers or paths for their stories so that storytellers could pick the best fitting one for their game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Weaver and Lucifer, let's go back and review about the Triat being building blocks of the universe in addition to vast spiritual presences. As Supernals rather than mere Celestines, they carry far more of the cosmos on their backs, and each is absolutely necessary. You could probably scrub Lucifer out from his own game and not actually end up losing a third of what makes the universe the universe, so that one fallen angel is way, way too small to be a part of the Triat. </div> </div> </div>The triat is a mythology. A bad retelling of creation, as telephoned down over generations of fera tribes. The Triat themselves are more conceptualizations, or cosmic forces, than specific entities; it's only through the garou mythology that they can properly explain them. So I'll concede that the comparisons are not basic one-for-one equivalencies. But nothing is lost from either Werewolf or Wraith by saying the Wyrm and Grandmother overlap, all that happens is that the two groups perceive their enemy differently. Which makes total sense when you consider that perception is pretty fluid in the umbra. As I suggested Grandmother is a facet or incarnation of the Wyrm, I'd pose that Lucifer too had a major role of a similar nature regarding the Weaver.<br /> <br /> And no, you could not remove Lucifer from his own game without losing a tremendous aspect of demon and the WoD's history. Yes, you could write something to replace him. But by that logic you could remove almost anything from almost anywhere, and this test becomes trivial.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the input, but I enjoy doing stuff like this. So I'm going to keep doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:18:52-07:00","id":591684,"title":"","content":"Personally I think Grandmother can't be the Wyrm (if there really is a being known as the Wyrm at all, rather than it being a personification imagined by the werewolves to explain all the various spirits and forces associated with the concept of entropy) because in Orpheus she is only recently awakened and interacting with the universe after untold ages of dormancy, if she ever previously interacted with it at all. The Wyrm (or the concepts that it's a stand-in for) has been active across a wide range of spiritual realms and in the physical world throughout history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:27:49-07:00","id":591692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=591575#post591575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building off that I think Lucifer and the Weaver may also have a great deal in common, being the same or related entities themselves:<br /> <br /> &quot;Weaver implanted mortals with three gifts, Dogma, Science, and Technology, in order to survive.&quot;<br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Weaver\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Weaver</a><br /> <br /> It was Lucifer who went on a campaign to encourage science &amp; technology after releasing his lieutenants from the Abyss resulted in the creation of the Earthbound. The Angels were the &quot;weavers&quot; of reality, crafting it all, and they went mad with rebellion when they abandoned the creator in an effort to prevent their works from being destroyed.<br /> <br /> &quot;mythology states that the Weaver grew tired of its order being destroyed by the Wyrm, and spun its webs to imprison the Wyrm and end its destruction.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lucifer encouraged disbelief, enforcing a loss of faith and banality throughout all of the world to prevent his fellow fallen from escaping the pit. He was a major cause of the spread of banality and the effects of the weaver's spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought a better comparison was actually God as the Weaver, seeing as how She created/built everything and had created a natural order which the Fallen violated when they revealed themselves to humans. With the idea that when She touched Creation in order to punish the Fallen (sorry if I'm getting the story confused, it's been a while since I read the source book), She essentially introduced destructive entropy.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a matter for an individual Storyteller to decide though. Whatever makes the best or most fun story wins. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:38:06-07:00","id":591714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=591692#post591692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought a better comparison was actually God as the Weaver, seeing as how She created/built everything and had created a natural order which the Fallen violated when they revealed themselves to humans. With the idea that when She touched Creation in order to punish the Fallen (sorry if I'm getting the story confused, it's been a while since I read the source book), She essentially introduced destructive entropy.<br /> <br /> Really, it's a matter for an individual Storyteller to decide though. Whatever makes the best or most fun story wins. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think God is all 3, the wyrm, weaver, and wyld. Which would fit with the Judeo-Christain inspirations by building a triadic relationship into their deity.<br /> <br /> It definitely is best for individual storytellers to work with, but that's part of why I like trying to build out these conspiracy theories! Assets for story-teller use. A lot of my friends enjoy crossing over, or combining the different games (White Wolf doesn't make that easy, but with a few trivial modifications it can happen). By being able to connect the disparate threads of different books' stories, you can find shared motivations that many of the different denizens of this world could unite behind. Werewolves could side with Stygians against Grandmother as a greater representation of the Wyrm. Changelings could join forces with Hunters in outrage against Lucifer (not the best plan, but I guarantee you could sell both on it). Black Spiral Dancers and Lasombra or Baali clan vampires could be serving as thralls to Earthbound intent on advancing the Wyrm's destruction of the world.<br /> <br /> I like being able to unite the different groups. For a game about the end of all things, it's satisfying to be able to draw together as many different threads as you can for the final climactic battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:44:42-07:00","id":591727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=591684#post591684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think Grandmother can't be the Wyrm (if there really is a being known as the Wyrm at all, rather than it being a personification imagined by the werewolves to explain all the various spirits and forces associated with the concept of entropy) because in Orpheus she is only recently awakened and interacting with the universe after untold ages of dormancy, if she ever previously interacted with it at all. The Wyrm (or the concepts that it's a stand-in for) has been active across a wide range of spiritual realms and in the physical world throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we don't really know much about Grandmother (at least I don't, maybe someone knows more). I agree with the Wyrm being a mythological entity more than a physical one, it's too big for this world. But the fera see things as agents of its destruction, and they could see powerful beings as specific manifestations or facets of the wyrm.<br /> <br /> But the Wyrm has been &quot;imprisoned&quot; for ages, only to be released when the apocalypse is upon us. Grandmother awakens at the dawn of that apocalypse, after the Red Star appears. Grandmother could be another aspect of the Wyrm, one that is now far more active. But Grandmother was active in the past as well, making the malfeans and other spectral monstrosities. So her actions have simply been few and far between, or subtle from her slumber beneath the Labyrinth. Which also fits with the wyrm, who has not had direct influence on the world except through agents and individual avatars or aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:59:02-07:00","id":591878,"title":"","content":"One major problem with the Lucifer = Weaver because Disbelief, it's that this politic of Lucifer regarding battling the Earthbounds it's relatively recent.<br /> The Weaver it's said to have entrapped the Wyrm in the second age, (the same age that the first killer did its first killing, according not only to myth, but also to the collective memory of the Mokole, the &quot;memory of Gaia&quot;). Even if this memory was wrong, Lucifer started the fight by encouraging religions, and there's no way that such doing could have caused &quot;the Escision&quot; of spirit and matter (which was caused somewhere around the time the Weaver went mad and imprisoned the Wyrm, according to legend). Specialy pondering that the Gauntlet existed WAY before christ.<br /> <br /> Besides, Lucifer it's no longer a &quot;multiversal entity&quot;. Lucifer fell with the rest of the Elohim in the day that God decided to destroy Eden, and stopped being an entity that exist in many layers of reality at once, to become a singular (if immensely powerful) being. That isn't like the Weaver, which it's a mad cosmic entity that exists in many layers of reality at once (albeit not necesarily in all of them)<br /> <br /> Apart from that, I also like the idea of the Triat being collectively God (it concords with the &quot;Gaia that was&quot; myth, and whit the fact that the Triad it's very powerfull in almost all of the Umbra and the material realm, but not in the Dark Umbra of the dead, which was created by the Halaku). <br /> Maybe God turn mad after the Fall, and stopped acting in armony. Anycase, this it's merely a fan-theory about Demon and the cWoD, and isn't compatible to everything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T18:29:03-07:00","id":592190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=591878#post591878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One major problem with the Lucifer = Weaver because Disbelief, it's that this politic of Lucifer regarding battling the Earthbounds it's relatively recent.<br /> The Weaver it's said to have entrapped the Wyrm in the second age, (the same age that the first killer did its first killing, according not only to myth, but also to the collective memory of the Mokole, the &quot;memory of Gaia&quot;). Even if this memory was wrong, Lucifer started the fight by encouraging religions, and there's no way that such doing could have caused &quot;the Escision&quot; of spirit and matter (which was caused somewhere around the time the Weaver went mad and imprisoned the Wyrm, according to legend). Specialy pondering that the Gauntlet existed WAY before christ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucifer's campaign of disbelief began... I think 1000AD or later?<br /> <br /> But yes, the imprisonment of the wyrm began at or just after the time of the fall if it happened at the same time that Cain slew Abel. I don't see why this discounts Lucifer as acting as a potent agent/aspect of the weaver though.... because he does do a lot to screw things up in that direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, Lucifer it's no longer a &quot;multiversal entity&quot;. Lucifer fell with the rest of the Elohim in the day that God decided to destroy Eden, and stopped being an entity that exist in many layers of reality at once, to become a singular (if immensely powerful) being. That isn't like the Weaver, which it's a mad cosmic entity that exists in many layers of reality at once (albeit not necesarily in all of them) </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that the Creator and the Triat (Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld) share identity. The Angels, as products of the Creator, are powerful spirits of one or all of those aspects. Back at the dawn of the World of Darkness stuff was crazy. The angels were made of divine essence, as were the souls of humans (though they got a greater part of that stuff, and it's why Lucifer tried his great experiment).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apart from that, I also like the idea of the Triat being collectively God (it concords with the &quot;Gaia that was&quot; myth, and whit the fact that the Triad it's very powerfull in almost all of the Umbra and the material realm, but not in the Dark Umbra of the dead, which was created by the Halaku).<br /> Maybe God turn mad after the Fall, and stopped acting in armony. Anycase, this it's merely a fan-theory about Demon and the cWoD, and isn't compatible to everything. </div> </div> </div>God went mad.... maybe a bit of multiple personality disorder? A shattered mind, where all the greater spirits/angels/souls are all parts of the whole.<br /> <br /> I don't think what's happening in the WoD cosmology is clean, neat, or clearly delineated. By saying Lucifer is an aspect of the Weaver, I'm also saying he's an independent entity as an angel. And also saying he is one of the many personalities of the larger Creator entity. Which went mad first, the Weaver or the Wyrm? Neither. They all went mad together because they're all one. And they went mad long before anything went wrong seeing as they split themselves into thousands of personalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T20:18:45-07:00","id":592250,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Time it's indeed manipulable at this level of the conspiration...wonder what would Lucifer say if he was told that he it's an aspect of the Spirit of Statism, and that his Rebelion was part of the scheme of around 1/3 of God to freeze Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T20:42:04-07:00","id":592264,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, I think what Saur Ops meant was that you could, like, right now, kill the Morningstar or otherwise force him out of his plans. The world would lose a major powerplayer, but not a fundamental concept. It would still be whole.<br /> <br /> Going by the definitions of the Weaver and assuming them correct, it is a fundamental block of the cosmos. If you &quot;kill&quot; it this same way, the world would crumble as Stasis itself turns to dust and ceases to exist.<br /> <br /> By the books, strictly, Lucifer seems to be a guy. A very old and powerful guy, indeed, with a hand over all human history, but still just a guy. Weaver is the supreme spirit of Stasis, and without it Stasis itself would die.<br /> <br /> That clarified, though, I don't see any problem with such interpretation. I wouldn't use that on most of my games, but is as valid as many others. I don't see many problems aside, maybe, the Fera would seem a bunch of fools for too much time. But almost every interpretation leaves someone for the fool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T20:43:02-07:00","id":592267,"title":"","content":"I found the Wyrm and Gorool are similar. Haven't heard of Grandmother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T20:47:14-07:00","id":592268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=592264#post592264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the books, strictly, Lucifer seems to be a guy. A very old and powerful guy, indeed, with a hand over all human history, but still just a guy. Weaver is the supreme spirit of Stasis, and without it Stasis itself would die.<br /> <br /> That clarified, though, I don't see any problem with such interpretation. I wouldn't use that on most of my games, but is as valid as many others. I don't see many problems aside, maybe, the Fera would seem a bunch of fools for too much time. But almost every interpretation leaves someone for the fool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if my argument were taken as fact, and Lucifer were a facet of the Weaver, killing Lucifer does not equate to killing the Weaver. All of the Weaver's facets would have to be destroyed to destroy it. I don't know such a thing is really possible given the types of things the Wyrm, Weaver, &amp; Wyld are. I don't think Lucifer would knowingly self-identify as an agent of the Weaver (even if he is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T00:13:10-07:00","id":592385,"title":"","content":"the wraith core rule book explicitly says that the wyrm and oblivion are different. that if the wyrm succeeded in its plans it would throw itssef at oblivion.<br /> <br /> that being said an old mummy book says that apophis and the wyrm are 