ainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=592190#post592190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lucifer's campaign of disbelief began... I think 1000AD or later?<br /> <br /> But yes, the imprisonment of the wyrm began at or just after the time of the fall if it happened at the same time that Cain slew Abel. I don't see why this discounts Lucifer as acting as a potent agent/aspect of the weaver though.... because he does do a lot to screw things up in that direction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd argue that the Creator and the Triat (Wyrm, Weaver, Wyld) share identity. The Angels, as products of the Creator, are powerful spirits of one or all of those aspects. Back at the dawn of the World of Darkness stuff was crazy. The angels were made of divine essence, as were the souls of humans (though they got a greater part of that stuff, and it's why Lucifer tried his great experiment).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> God went mad.... maybe a bit of multiple personality disorder? A shattered mind, where all the greater spirits/angels/souls are all parts of the whole.<br /> <br /> I don't think what's happening in the WoD cosmology is clean, neat, or clearly delineated. By saying Lucifer is an aspect of the Weaver, I'm also saying he's an independent entity as an angel. And also saying he is one of the many personalities of the larger Creator entity. Which went mad first, the Weaver or the Wyrm? Neither. They all went mad together because they're all one. And they went mad long before anything went wrong seeing as they split themselves into thousands of personalities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've logged in just to upvote this comment. Well done, love the idea. More so, as it is said explicitly in Demon, the angels were not only the creators of the universe; they were the principles of it all, the physic, biological, chemical laws themselves. And i love it being linked this way to other mythologies. What we see of the angels is only our own vision and interpretation ef the realities they were/are -though warped-. Love it, also, considering Lucifer an aspect (or the most potent aspect) of the Weaver. Malkes perfect sense. Also, i agree thoroughly with Lucifer not knowing he is part of the Weaver... because for him, there is none. I mean, the Triat as a whole is the God he knew, he loved, he was part of. So he wouldn't bother about the ideas the flesh creatures living on earth would have as cosmic - Godly beings. He is who he is. Nice ideas man!!<br /> <br /> Oh, and by the way: you definitely CANNOT erase Lucifer from Demon the Fallen. He is the reason behind the Fell of the ENTIRE universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":1349,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","user":"Phersus","date":".  Grammar and stuff. Still making mistakes, though :/ 07-17-2015, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T05:43:46-07:00","id":594702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=592914#post592914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It also says that Grandmother is not Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than being the force of Oblivion, she's specifically the Grand Maw: a primal-location-god-thing at the bottom of the universe, from which Oblivion appears to emanate as a force.<br /> <br /> That the Grand Maw is described as being sentient, and a being as well as a location, and perhaps even the 'dark twin' of God always sounded to me like one of the Primordials/Yozi. Could she be the mirror of Gaia? She's described as wanting to devour in order to create again. She is a primordial manifestation of the Vagina Dentata.<br /> <br /> Of course, God is pretty much vanished from the World of Darkness (or at least fragmented). But what if God, displeased with the state of Creation and wishing to make it anew, now fragmented, had created Oblivion from a fragment of Her consciousness? Sort of like the Shadow of God.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm, being active, I've always assumed as being an avatar of God/the universe (a cog in the Prime machine), while Oblivion is a force of unmaking as the cosmos drains out through the Great Maw (i.e., the direction of movement of Prime through the machine), perhaps to be recycled elsewhere.<br /> <br /> If you see God as all Prime, and the universe as a wheel/Prime machine, God cycles round, being destroyed and recreated, devouring and rebirthing Herself like the Ouroboros. Yahweh, Lucifer, the Triat, etc, are all merely lesser manifestations of the intricate Prime machine. They're the cogs. Dynamism, Entropy and Stasis are merely the movements of the Prime's flow through that machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-18-2015, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:31:10-07:00","id":594878,"title":"","content":"I would also like to point out that the Second Age had the Shattering as described in DtF, wherein the entire cosmos was altered and lessend. Before things such as Michael's sword, existed on several different levels, multifaceted like a diamond. After the Shattering though, using Michael's Sword, each facet became a singular entity in this case a sword and an anomoly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T17:25:34-07:00","id":595158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/591553-the-wyrm-grandmother?p=594878#post594878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like to point out that the Second Age had the Shattering as described in DtF, wherein the entire cosmos was altered and lessend. Before things such as Michael's sword, existed on several different levels, multifaceted like a diamond. After the Shattering though, using Michael's Sword, each facet became a singular entity in this case a sword and an anomoly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The infinitely complex and multifaceted great machine we call the universe has eroded from apathy and time. Now it runs more like Al Bundy's Dodge.... the end is definitely near, and any beauty that was left in the world is probably dying or falling apart along with it. Part of the horror of demon is seeing how much of your work was left to rot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}